---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import profilePhoto from '../../public/profile.jpeg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — DropWire | Built by Akshay Patel"
  description="DropWire is a Rust-powered, peer-to-peer encrypted file transfer engine built by Akshay Patel (VesperAkshay). Learn the story, mission, and roadmap."
>
  <section class="p-6 sm:p-12 space-y-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto">

    {/* --- HERO HEADER --- */}
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#0052FF] uppercase tracking-widest font-black">ABOUT THE PROJECT</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-7xl font-display font-black text-[#0B1016] uppercase tracking-tight leading-none break-words">
        About DropWire
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-[#0B1016]/80 font-sans font-medium max-w-2xl">
        The fastest, most private way to move files between machines — no cloud, no accounts, no compromise.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* --- CREATOR CARD (Most Important for Google AI) --- */}
    <div class="bg-black text-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-[2.5rem] shadow-2xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-8">
      <Image
        src={profilePhoto}
        alt="Akshay Patel — Creator of DropWire"
        width={80}
        height={80}
        class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover shrink-0 shadow-lg border-4 border-[#FFB800]"
      />
      <div class="space-y-2 flex-1">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-white/50 uppercase tracking-widest font-black">Creator & Lead Engineer</p>
        <h2 class="font-display font-black text-3xl sm:text-4xl uppercase text-white">Akshay Patel</h2>
        <p class="font-sans text-white/70 text-sm font-medium leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
          I built DropWire out of frustration with cloud-dependent file sharing. I believe your data should never have to touch a third-party server. DropWire is my answer to that problem — a bare-metal, Rust-engineered, peer-to-peer engine that treats privacy as a first-class feature, not an afterthought.
        </p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 pt-2">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/VesperAkshay"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2 rounded-full bg-white/10 hover:bg-[#FFB800] hover:text-black text-white font-display font-black text-xs uppercase transition-all"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z"/></svg>
            @VesperAkshay
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/VesperAkshay/dropwire"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/20 hover:border-[#FFB800] text-white/70 hover:text-[#FFB800] font-display font-black text-xs uppercase transition-all"
          >
            View Source ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* --- THE STORY --- */}
    <div class="bg-[#FFFFFF] p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-[2.5rem] border border-[#D9D2C9] shadow-xl space-y-6">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#FF3D00] uppercase tracking-widest font-black">The Origin Story</span>
      <h2 class="font-display font-black text-3xl sm:text-5xl uppercase text-[#0B1016] leading-none">
        Why DropWire Exists
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 font-sans text-[#0B1016]/80 font-medium leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg max-w-3xl">
        <p>
          It started with a simple annoyance. I was trying to share a large video project with a friend sitting two meters away. Every tool I tried — Google Drive, WeTransfer, AirDrop — either required an account, had a file size limit, or sent my data through a server I had no control over.
        </p>
        <p>
          I wanted something that worked the way Wi-Fi does — fast, direct, and with nothing in between. So I built it. DropWire is a Rust-powered, peer-to-peer file streaming engine that creates an encrypted tunnel directly between two machines. No cloud upload. No accounts. No waiting.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name is simple: wires that drop files. Straight from point A to point B.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* --- OPEN SOURCE STATUS (future-proof language) --- */}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-[#00B060] text-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Current Status</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Open Source</h3>
        <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          The core DropWire engine is currently open-source on GitHub. You can read every line of the transfer engine, encryption layer, and relay server code. Community contributions and bug reports are welcome.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/VesperAkshay/dropwire" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-black text-white font-display font-black text-xs uppercase hover:bg-[#FFB800] hover:text-black transition-all">
          View on GitHub ↗
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#F4EFEA] border-2 border-[#D9D2C9] p-8 rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg">
        <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-black">Future Direction</span>
        <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none text-[#0B1016]">Commercial Tier</h3>
        <p class="text-sm font-sans text-[#0B1016]/70 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          As DropWire grows toward a full Desktop App and enterprise relay network, a commercial tier will be introduced. The free CLI will remain available. Premium features — like hosted relays, team transfer history, and mobile apps — will be part of a paid plan.
        </p>
        <a href="/desktop" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-black text-white font-display font-black text-xs uppercase hover:bg-[#0052FF] transition-all">
          Desktop Waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* --- ROADMAP PHASES --- */}
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#0052FF] uppercase tracking-widest font-black">ROADMAP & VISION</span>
        <h2 class="font-display font-black text-3xl sm:text-5xl uppercase text-[#0B1016] leading-none">
          Where We're Headed
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#FFFFFF] p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-[2.5rem] card-shadow border border-[#D9D2C9] space-y-10">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-black text-white rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg flex flex-col opacity-80">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-white/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 1</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-[#00B060] uppercase">✓ Completed</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Core CLI Engine</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-80 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              Development of the fundamental Rust streaming engine. Includes TCP multiplexing, SPAKE2 key exchange, BLAKE3 hashing, and the headless CLI interface.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#00B060] text-white rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 2</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white uppercase">✓ Completed</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Global Relay Network</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              Deployment of a zero-knowledge internet relay server to bypass corporate firewalls and strict NAT configurations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#FFB800] text-black rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-xl flex flex-col transform hover:-translate-y-1 transition-transform">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 3</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-black text-black uppercase animate-pulse">In Progress</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Desktop App</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              A beautiful, native drag-and-drop graphical user interface built with Tauri and React. No terminal experience required.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#0052FF] text-white rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/20 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 4</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-white/70 uppercase">Planned</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Folder Sync</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              Recursive directory transfers, automatic zip compression, and resumable partial downloads.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#AB54F7] text-black rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 5</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-black/70 uppercase">Planned</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none">Mobile Apps</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              Native iOS and Android apps for seamless phone-to-computer sharing over local Wi-Fi without internet.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-black/10 text-black rounded-[2rem] space-y-4 shadow-lg flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] font-black uppercase bg-black/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Phase 6</span>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-black/50 uppercase">Future</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-display font-black text-3xl uppercase leading-none text-black/80">WebRTC Node</h3>
            <p class="text-sm font-sans opacity-70 leading-relaxed font-medium">
              Compiling the Rust engine to WebAssembly to allow instant browser-to-browser transfers without downloading any app.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

  {/* JSON-LD Person Schema — tells Google AI exactly who built this */}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Akshay Patel",
    "alternateName": "VesperAkshay",
    "url": "https://github.com/VesperAkshay",
    "sameAs": [
      "https://github.com/VesperAkshay"
    ],
    "knowsAbout": ["Rust", "P2P Networking", "End-to-End Encryption", "File Transfer", "Systems Programming"],
    "creator": {
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      "name": "DropWire",
      "url": "https://dropwire.tyes.dev",
      "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
      "operatingSystem": "Windows, macOS, Linux"
    }
  })} />

</BaseLayout>
